    {
      "id": "27e2682c-d468-4a78-905a-56a830204bba",
      "name": "Overview Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1168,
        -240
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 648,
        "height": 760,
        "content": "## Turn a Telegram message into an approved Facebook + Instagram post\n\nFor small businesses and agencies that post image content every week and want a human to approve every post before it goes live.\n\n### How it works\n1. Message your Telegram bot with a post idea.\n2. Gemini writes a caption and an image prompt using your brand context.\n3. You approve the caption in Telegram, or tap Regenerate.\n4. Cloudflare Flux creates the image, which is converted to JPEG (Instagram requires it) and hosted on Google Drive.\n5. You approve the image.\n6. The post goes to Facebook, then to Instagram (container, status check, publish), and is logged in Google Sheets.\n\nAfter one regeneration the workflow flags the request for a manual look instead of looping.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. Telegram: create a bot with @BotFather and add the credential.\n2. Gemini: Header Auth credential, name `x-goog-api-key`, value your key.\n3. Cloudflare Workers AI: Header Auth, name `Authorization`, value `Bearer <token>`.\n4. Google Drive and Google Sheets: connect your accounts. Create a sheet with a tab named Log and columns timestamp, prompt, image_url, status.\n5. Facebook Graph API: add a credential with a Page access token.\n6. Fill in the Set Brand Context node (Page ID, Instagram Business account ID) and your Cloudflare account ID in the Generate Image URL.\n\nStep-by-step guide and free PDF checklist: https://uzzaman.dev/guides/instagram-facebook-auto-posting-setup/\n\n### Customization tips\n- Edit `brand_context` to match your tone.\n- Swap the image model by changing the Generate Image URL.\n- Raise the limit in Under Retry Cap? to allow more regenerations.\n- Drive images are shared publicly so Meta can fetch them. Use a dedicated folder."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "215842ab-c1cd-4944-afe4-982b3d5c7cff",
      "name": "Step 1 Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -480,
        -208
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 440,
        "content": "### 1. Receive the request\nThe bot ignores empty messages and commands. Set Brand Context holds your business name, tone and the Facebook Page and Instagram IDs."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b8205d26-ee7c-4d65-8aea-0b2548ac4169",
      "name": "Step 2 Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        112,
        -48
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 620,
        "height": 300,
        "content": "### 2. Draft and approve the caption\nGemini returns JSON with an image prompt and caption (retries 3 times). You approve or regenerate in Telegram."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c8521f48-902e-40cb-8304-120761708cda",
      "name": "Step 3 Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        208,
        288
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1000,
        "height": 420,
        "content": "### 3. Generate and host the image\nFlux creates a 1:1 image, it is resized to JPEG, uploaded to Drive and made public. Meta fetches images from a URL, it does not accept uploads."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c76c4b91-9555-4368-90a1-f51b5f011230",
      "name": "Step 4 Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        192,
        752
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 800,
        "height": 252,
        "content": "### 4. Approve the image\nA preview is sent to Telegram. Approve to publish, or regenerate."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "09e315c1-eaf9-4a3b-92e9-57f3c5181fe6",
      "name": "Step 5 Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1280,
        368
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 280,
        "height": 214,
        "content": "### 5. Publish to Facebook\nPosts the photo to your Page with the caption."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "82d0d870-cb1f-4309-932b-50d29d3d8662",
      "name": "Step 6 Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1152,
        720
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1100,
        "height": 270,
        "content": "### 6. Create the Instagram container\nInstagram needs a container first. The workflow checks its status every 10 seconds, up to 12 times, then stops with an error."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "fc905353-267a-4549-a4fd-e2502a17ece5",
      "name": "Step 7 Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1904,
        320
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 460,
        "height": 220,
        "content": "### 7. Publish and log\nPublishes to Instagram, then appends a row to your Log sheet."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "db3c34e7-a1d0-4d95-aba2-daac594cd717",
      "name": "Step 8 Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        736,
        1024
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 700,
        "height": 232,
        "content": "### Regenerate or flag\nRegenerate sends the request back to Gemini once. After that, Telegram gets a message asking for a manual review."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "6a17cbf3-5407-4706-b8fd-82aa2fa86344",
      "name": "Setup Pack Note",
